Subject: winex11: add bounded scrolling after a matching end signal

Record the last 100 ms of accepted fine-grained scrolling or middle-button
movement. Start continued movement only after a matching stop report or a
moving middle-button release. Silence only abandons the recorded sequence.

Reduce velocity over the complete elapsed time but calculate output for no
more than the latest 16 ms. Limit each message to 30 wheel units and each axis
to 480 units for the complete coast. Discard missed frames and excess whole
movement instead of replaying them later.

Keep delayed messages at the window and screen point where movement began.
Cancel on new pointer, button, key, focus, grab, device, or scroll input.

See notes/ABLETON-WINE-POINTER-GESTURES.md for the formula, constants, and
manual safety acceptance tests.
